---
description: Prevent command injection vulnerabilities when executing shell commands
alwaysApply: true
---

command-injection-prevention:

- Avoid executing shell commands with user input when possible
- Use safe APIs that don't invoke a shell (e.g., child_process.execFile instead of exec)
- Never concatenate user input into shell commands
- Use argument arrays instead of string concatenation
- Validate and whitelist allowed inputs
- Escape shell metacharacters if shell execution is unavoidable

Dangerous patterns:
```javascript
exec(`rm -rf ${userPath}`);
spawn('sh', ['-c', `cat ${filename}`]);
```

Safe patterns:
```javascript
execFile('rm', ['-rf', userPath]);
spawn('cat', [filename]);
```
